1
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:13,847
What's up?

2
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,725
"What's up"?
You just left us. That's what's up.

3
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:18,727
Yeah.

4
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:20,854
I'm sorry.

5
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:22,355
Listen.

6
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,734
You're quitting the clinic, aren't you?

7
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,110
It's all good.

8
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:32,157
I'm gonna think about everything
carefully.

9
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,577
You should get some rest.

10
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:37,662
It'll be fine.

11
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,456
Uh-huh.

12
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,082
Yeah, good night.

13
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,259
Thank you very much, sir.

14
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:53,303
Thank you. Good night.

15
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:45,165
THE HAND OF GOD

16
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,334
Arata?

17
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,003
Mom.

18
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:53,173
Oh my goodness.

19
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:55,550
You're making another one already?

20
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,926
The competition is soon.

21
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:00,430
Sayuri!

22
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:02,015
Where'd you go?

23
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,893
You left everything out again.

24
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:07,020
Honey, if you don't stop,

25
00:03:07,103 --> 00:03:09,272
Papa and Grandma will be mad at you again.

26
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:12,066
<i>I have no desire</i>

27
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,236
<i>to stoke any conflict</i>
<i>or competition within my family.</i>

28
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:18,865
So please, I'm asking you all,

29
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:22,035
let's not turn this
into some kind of family civil war.

30
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:25,330
This new venture of mine
shouldn't be making headlines.

31
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,748
But sir, this is news.

32
00:03:26,831 --> 00:03:29,417
Aren't you essentially asking
for your daughter to step down?

33
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,962
No, I've never asked her to step back
from her duties as a doctor.

34
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:36,424
<i>That said, I founded</i>
<i>the Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic,</i>

35
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,927
<i>and… and I gave it its name.</i>

36
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:41,095
<i>All I'm asking</i>
<i>is that she give the name back.</i>

37
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,347
Excuse me.

38
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,934
<i>In light of this request,</i>
<i>Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic</i>

39
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,936
<i>issued a statement</i>
<i>through its legal counsel,</i>

40
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:51,439
<i>stating that it has no plans whatsoever</i>
<i>to change its name.</i>

41
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:56,319
<i>The rift between father and daughter</i>
<i>seems unlikely to mend anytime soon.</i>

42
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:58,112
Oh my God, you're leaving?

43
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,781
Did you find another clinic to take you?

44
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:02,742
I found a place that's hiring,
so I'll be interviewing there.

45
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:04,535
- What?
- Yeah, I'll send you the info.

46
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,704
Welcome back, Numata.

47
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:10,833
I gotta say, I don't get it.

48
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:13,795
Why would you come back to work
in the middle of this crisis?

49
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,967
Are you also going somewhere else?

50
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,176
Me?

51
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,681
- You won't tell anyone?
- I won't.

52
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:26,140
- Cross your heart?
- Yeah.

53
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:28,476
For sure. I'm on it.

54
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,479
I don't think you can keep a secret.

55
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,860
You're holding a press conference?

56
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:41,990
Director, we were advised to wait
by the legal department.

57
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:44,409
We'll lose staff if we wait any longer.

58
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:46,577
Won't we?

59
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,162
I'm afraid she's right.

60
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:53,001
I'd like it scheduled for today.
It doesn't matter where we hold it.

61
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,043
Director…

62
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:57,463
And before the conference,
I need to meet someone.

63
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,340
Get the car ready, please.

64
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:16,524
I'm sorry. I… I'm Dr. Tohyama,
and I was hoping to speak to you.

65
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:18,818
What do you want?

66
00:05:19,777 --> 00:05:22,238
- I'd love to hear more.
- Don't get me started.

67
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,782
- You're all encouraging him.
- Come on, please.

68
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,617
As if I need it.

69
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:30,663
You wouldn't know it from looking,
but he's a huge mama's boy.

70
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:33,499
Come on, lay off it.
Talking like I'm still a child.

71
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,752
Aw, age has nothing to do with it.

72
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,421
A man doesn't grow out of his nature
just like that.

73
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:43,384
Though I admit, in your case,
you've taken loyalty to the extreme.

74
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:44,719
Mm! Oh, you think?

75
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:46,429
Oh, I know it.

76
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:48,848
You were heir to a construction empire.

77
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:50,641
But no, you didn't want any of it.

78
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:54,020
You wanted to carry on
your late mother's name and family line.

79
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:57,190
He has a point.

80
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,150
Goodness.

81
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:02,195
Didn't your father object
when you walked away from his name?

82
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:04,739
Oh yes, "object" is putting it lightly.

83
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:05,782
I was only a child.

84
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:08,034
But I didn't care.

85
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:11,287
You see,
there was no love lost between us.

86
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:14,290
It's funny how things work out.

87
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:18,044
Hmm? What do you mean?

88
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:20,922
Just that you turned your back
on your father,

89
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:23,883
and now your daughter Rin
is about to do the same thing.

90
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:28,054
Hmm…

91
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:31,224
You know? She's right.

92
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,104
It is funny.

93
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,939
- Mm-hmm.
- That's well said.

94
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:38,981
It is!

95
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:58,000
Stop!
Why are you doing that to Mom's birds?

96
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,962
I want you to forget about that woman.

97
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,631
Killed herself in the Odajima house.
I can't.

98
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:05,591
No! These birds were special to her.

99
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,427
She was a liar. Don't defend her.

100
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,512
Stop it! She wasn't a liar! She wasn't!

101
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:11,973
Her face was as fake as her background.

102
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,267
You know she had plastic surgery?

103
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,316
Thank you so much.

104
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:25,486
I appreciate you all being here today.

105
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:29,699
I called this press conference
to provide clarity.

106
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,659
To take responsibility and to be a leader.

107
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:36,164
I owe an explanation
to those who have supported the clinic

108
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:37,415
over the years.

109
00:07:37,915 --> 00:07:39,208
So thank you.

110
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:41,711
I know this was on short notice.

111
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:45,006
Well, well, well, "Hand of God."
Let's see what you've got.

112
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,216
<i>I have to imagine</i>
<i>what you're mostly interested in</i>

113
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,510
<i>are all of the rumors and speculations</i>

114
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:50,678
<i>flying around online</i>

115
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:52,555
<i>about my father and Tohyama Clinic.</i>

116
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,308
But I will not be addressing that.

117
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,311
This press conference
is about something else.

118
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:01,898
Ms. Tohyama, what do you mean?
You don't have any comment at this time?

119
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:02,815
Interesting.

120
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:06,777
What I wanted to talk to you about

121
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,530
is how we'll be running things
from now on.

122
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:12,909
And also, the direction we intend to take.

123
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:15,077
<i>The clinic's future is bright.</i>

124
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:20,374
Fumi Numata.

125
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,838
<i>That's a name</i>
<i>I imagine many of you recognize.</i>

126
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:31,385
She was accused of medical malpractice
and criminal negligence

127
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:34,555
<i>following the tragic death</i>
<i>of the model Kana Kokubun.</i>

128
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:38,267
Nowhere to hide, Fumi.

129
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:41,270
However, the Tohyama Clinic and I
are very proud

130
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:44,148
to now be able to announce to you

131
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,901
that we have signed Dr. Numata
on to our team.

132
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:48,778
What?

133
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:52,698
There is more to Ms. Kokubun's story.

134
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:55,993
She was suffering
from early-onset breast cancer.

135
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:59,205
<i>In order to treat her,</i>

136
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:02,083
<i>I advised her to have</i>
<i>her silicone breast implants removed.</i>

137
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:04,877
<i>She categorically refused.</i>

138
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:08,381
<i>Being a model, I can only imagine</i>

139
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:11,384
<i>how difficult the thought</i>
<i>of changing her body was for her</i>

140
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:13,636
<i>and how painful her decision was.</i>

141
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:18,307
Our next step was to test the possibility

142
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,726
of seeing if we could find her
new replacement implants

143
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,853
and if they could be made more safe.

144
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,649
<i>My team and I did our best,</i>

145
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:30,653
<i>but her condition degraded</i>
<i>quite quickly, unfortunately.</i>

146
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,657
<i>She was rushed to the Medical University,</i>

147
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:40,496
where Dr. Numata chose to prioritize
saving Ms. Kokubun's life above all else.

148
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,332
<i>She removed Ms. Kokubun's implants.</i>

149
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:47,712
As a doctor, it's obvious
her decision was the right one.

150
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:48,796
I would've done the same.

151
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:52,466
<i>What happened was a tragedy.</i>

152
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:54,218
<i>I do not blame Dr. Numata.</i>

153
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:56,887
In fact,
some of the responsibility is mine.

154
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,059
It's time that I admit my fault.

155
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:24,540
I apologize
to Ms. Kokubun's family and fans.

156
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,459
On behalf of the clinic,

157
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,629
I'm so sorry for what happened.

158
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:32,798
I'm sorry.

159
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,009
Please forgive us.

160
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:39,347
<i>Dr. Tohyama, can you tell us more?</i>

161
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:42,600
Will Dr. Numata
be issuing another formal apology?

162
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:48,981
- So what are you going to do about Rin?
- What do you mean?

163
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:54,695
Listen, you know I've been
a big supporter of your business.

164
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:57,490
For a long time too. That won't change.

165
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,409
I'll do everything in my power
to help you.

166
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:02,161
However,

167
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:05,373
this very public spat with your daughter
isn't going over well.

168
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:09,543
And what's more, it's not a good look.

169
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:10,670
I agree.

170
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:14,965
You know, Rin used to come over
and play with Sara when she was little.

171
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,676
She's a family friend.

172
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:19,720
When Sara was diagnosed
with juvenile glaucoma,

173
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,514
Rin was always there for her.

174
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:23,891
She was so caring and attentive.

175
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,897
Why not let her use the family name?

176
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:32,316
Then you can bury the hatchet.

177
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,404
<i>Dr. Numata is talented.</i>

178
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:38,155
She's a very skilled surgeon.

179
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:42,243
Her philosophy
is in line with the clinic's.

180
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:44,745
<i>She combines empathy with genius.</i>

181
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:49,750
And by serving our patients
not just as clients but as human beings,

182
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:53,879
the Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic
will undoubtedly soar to new heights.

183
00:11:56,048 --> 00:11:57,341
I truly believe that.

184
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:04,265
Seriously? What a joke.

185
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:07,810
So…

186
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,771
You wanted me to address the rumors?

187
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,190
I've said what I came here to say.

188
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,327
Hey, I'm home.

189
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,795
Fumi, do you want something to eat?

190
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,507
No, I'm good, but… what's going on?

191
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,344
You're just gonna ignore what Mom wanted?

192
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,305
What?

193
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:47,558
Mom didn't want you
to be a plastic surgeon anymore.

194
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:50,561
You can't just go back to work.

195
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:52,563
I thought it through. Don't worry.

196
00:12:52,646 --> 00:12:53,856
Then tell me how.

197
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:56,400
How can you go back?

198
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:59,278
Standing in front of Mom's ashes
before going back to work.

199
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,532
Takeru's got a point.

200
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:07,369
If you're going back to work there,
you owe us an explanation.

201
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,705
Takeru gave you her savings so you could--

202
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,248
Now hang on.

203
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:15,377
Mom saved that money over 30 years,

204
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:17,838
and she never touched it.

205
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,926
What makes you think I can use it?

206
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:24,762
Huh?

207
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:27,223
You're just like her.

208
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:28,891
Stubborn as hell.

209
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:31,727
Takeru.

210
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:35,314
I know how Mom felt about it.
You don't have to lecture me.

211
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:36,565
I--

212
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:38,317
Don't walk away. Hey!

213
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:39,944
Takeru…

214
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:42,571
Screw this.

215
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,628
<i>Cool.</i>

216
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:00,631
So you're just gonna
drink your problems away.

217
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,007
Good idea.

218
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:04,927
Yeah. What else am I gonna do?

219
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:08,764
Explain my relationship to the chairman
to a teenager?

220
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,099
I don't think so.

221
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:13,269
But like…
couldn't you just leave the clinic?

222
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,478
Then it'd be fine.

223
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:17,231
I obviously can't. That's exactly
what the chairman would want.

224
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,483
Who the hell cares what he thinks?

225
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:23,153
'Cause you were, like, all gung ho
on taking Rin down, right?

226
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,657
It's just complicated.

227
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,242
Um, can I get another drink?

228
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:29,285
Sure thing.

229
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:30,828
Hey.

230
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:32,913
Why don't you do a DNA test?

231
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,499
No. What? Why would I do a test?

232
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,877
- You know I have evidence.
- What if he's not your dad?

233
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,836
Huh?

234
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,963
What if this "absolute worst" doctor

235
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:42,298
was somebody else?

236
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:47,553
Because then you'd have no reason
to help Rin, would you?

237
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:55,519
DIRECTOR RIN, RUI, HIKITA

238
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,813
NUMATA

239
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:00,691
TOHYAMA COSMETIC SURGERY CLINIC
DOCTOR NUMATA

240
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:03,944
Endoscopic surgery.

241
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:06,697
We're gonna start doing that here?

242
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,700
Yes, it's important for you
to have a signature procedure.

243
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:13,704
Doctors who have one
are much easier to promote.

244
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:15,581
We'll have it up and running by next week.

245
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:17,750
Next week?

246
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,127
The boss is bossy today.

247
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:24,006
The boss has a good head for business.

248
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:32,014
What was he like?

249
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,893
What was the chairman like as a father?

250
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:39,188
Huh?

251
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,607
I just…

252
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:43,859
I live with my stepdad.

253
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:49,615
So you don't have a biological father,
and… I don't have one either.

254
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,327
Oh, I understand.

255
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,496
I was

256
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:59,375
wondering what life was like
with your dad.

257
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,502
What was it like?

258
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:05,714
My parents had a hard time
conceiving a child.

259
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,717
That's why they adopted me.

260
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,596
Growing up, it was tough.

261
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,974
The other kids made fun of me.

262
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:18,769
Dad… he had a show on TV,

263
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:22,356
and he broadcast a photo of himself
pre-plastic surgery.

264
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,441
And it was so obvious.

265
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:26,527
We looked nothing alike.

266
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:32,658
I mean, of course,
I couldn't look like him.

267
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,369
I'm not really his.

268
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:50,134
Hey, Takeru.

269
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:52,136
Are you up yet?

270
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,973
I won't make you go to school
if you don't want.

271
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,517
But would you at least eat this?

272
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,477
I'm leaving the <i>omurice </i>here.

273
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,147
Make sure you eat it, okay?

274
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:06,650
I can't take it anymore.

275
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,737
He's still up there in his room.

276
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:15,117
Well, that does happen sometimes.

277
00:17:15,993 --> 00:17:17,286
Yes, it does.

278
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:21,081
- Okay. Let's continue. Good.
- Right.

279
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,041
Next name?

280
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,125
It's…

281
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,252
Oh! It's Arata Tohyama!

282
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,212
Okay. Thick envelope!

283
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,923
- Ah! Yes! Thank you, thank you, thank you!
- Thank you!

284
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,969
Oh, Fumi's calling.

285
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:37,347
Yeah, Makihara here.

286
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:42,019
Oh, we were just getting ready
to write thank-you cards.

287
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,855
Hmm? The address?

288
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,257
I'm glad you came over.

289
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,467
Come in.

290
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:19,306
Hey, Sara.

291
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:20,974
What can I do for you?

292
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:25,813
Mm, I was thinking about, you know,

293
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,357
maybe getting
the new ultrasound treatment.

294
00:18:29,024 --> 00:18:32,236
Oh, and I've been so tired lately.

295
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,278
I want an IV drip.

296
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,281
No problem.

297
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,533
Right this way.

298
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,544
<i>How about I get you a drink?</i>

299
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,170
Hang on.

300
00:18:51,296 --> 00:18:52,422
Why were you there?

301
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,550
At my mother's wake?

302
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:56,009
Hmm?

303
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:59,930
Oh. Well, she was an acquaintance.
I knew her, is all.

304
00:19:00,013 --> 00:19:01,557
You knew her?

305
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,643
You dated her once, right?

306
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:08,939
What is all this?
That's a strange thing to ask.

307
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:10,983
Dr. Tohyama, are you my father?

308
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,369
All right.

309
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:24,204
Let's say that I was.

310
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:26,456
What would you want from me?

311
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:30,169
- What would I want from you?
- Yes.

312
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:31,545
My daughter and I

313
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:34,256
are about to enter a legal battle
for the Tohyama name.

314
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:37,676
You're an employee of hers.
You might use any of this against me.

315
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:40,262
I don't care about your fight.
It's not like that.

316
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:42,890
That's not why I'm here.

317
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:45,267
I just….

318
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,394
Just what?

319
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:49,313
Uh…

320
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:51,732
My mother was in…

321
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:56,028
She went through a lot.

322
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:59,281
And I wanna know
what caused her to suffer like she did.

323
00:20:02,659 --> 00:20:05,787
Grandfather's investing
in your dad's new clinic, apparently.

324
00:20:06,371 --> 00:20:07,539
Oh. I see.

325
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:11,668
Better not lose. You know?

326
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:14,087
Huh?

327
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:18,508
I'd have to go to so much trouble
to find a new personal doctor if you did.

328
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:24,848
What Grandpa said to your dad at dinner

329
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:28,518
was that you should be able
to use your Tohyama name.

330
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,899
Now, what do you think
your dad said to him?

331
00:20:36,568 --> 00:20:39,488
He'd rather be dead than let you!

332
00:20:39,571 --> 00:20:42,783
It was so funny, Rin.

333
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:53,126
Why do you think it's funny?

334
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:58,048
None of this would be happening…

335
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:02,511
if you hadn't broken your promise.

336
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:04,096
What do you mean?

337
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:07,391
You told him about the accident,
didn't you? I know you did.

338
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:16,441
Here's what I propose.

339
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:19,987
You leave your job at Tohyama,
and I'll tell you what I know.

340
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,114
It doesn't make a difference where I work.

341
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,198
I have a right to know!

342
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,283
It may be your right,

343
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:26,910
but protecting the secret
your mother entrusted to me

344
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,203
is my responsibility.

345
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,545
This is a waste of time. Excuse me.

346
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,299
I'll see you there.

347
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:43,969
At my new clinic, that is.

348
00:21:45,846 --> 00:21:46,805
What are you saying?

349
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:49,224
What I'm saying is that one day,

350
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:51,435
I'm hoping you take over as director.

351
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:54,771
Huh? That's never gonna happen! No way!

352
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:55,856
It was your fingers.

353
00:21:57,941 --> 00:22:01,695
When I took your hand,
I just had a feeling.

354
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:03,697
Intuition.

355
00:22:04,781 --> 00:22:06,450
I want you to be my successor.

356
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:15,959
What is so funny?

357
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:21,256
You think I said something to your dad
about you, don't you? But I didn't.

358
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:24,843
No, because if I told people what you did,

359
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:27,429
you'd be out of a job so fast
your head would spin.

360
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:30,682
But then I wouldn't be able to use you
as my own private doctor.

361
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:34,353
And that would be so dull, right?

362
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:38,106
You were at the hotel with him.

363
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,317
He invited me out to eat dinner, sure.

364
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:44,488
But we didn't talk about you.

365
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:51,828
You're gonna have to pay the price
for my eyes until the day you die.

366
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:55,874
My eyes! Why can't I see?

367
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:42,421
Director, may I have a word?

368
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:43,880
Sure.

369
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,723
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

370
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,311
Did the chairman poach you?

371
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:05,652
Well, it can't stay a secret forever.

372
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:07,571
He offered me a job.

373
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,535
You never valued me here.

374
00:24:14,828 --> 00:24:17,664
I thought you'd make
me director of the Ginza clinic,

375
00:24:17,747 --> 00:24:19,374
but you didn't want to promote me.

376
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:23,170
You just wanted to use me
to draw in female clients.

377
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:25,464
I was a figurehead,

378
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:30,051
never getting the real prestige,
and being stuck with the boring surgeries.

379
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:31,136
I'm done.

380
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:34,139
Do you think the chairman
will treat you any different?

381
00:24:34,222 --> 00:24:35,807
Well…

382
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,436
that's the thing about us.

383
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,979
We're all cut from the same cloth.

384
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:44,232
We cosmetic surgeons,
we work so hard in med school,

385
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:48,236
only to throw our integrity out the window
and chase money instead.

386
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:51,823
In the end,

387
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:55,702
I was presented with two offers,
and I made a choice.

388
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,247
Thanks for everything.

389
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:17,098
Excuse me, Director.

390
00:25:27,692 --> 00:25:29,819
Hey, Numata, bad day?

391
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:32,447
Oh. You clocking out already?

392
00:25:32,531 --> 00:25:34,991
She's just going to use you
in my place, you know.

393
00:25:35,575 --> 00:25:36,409
Sorry?

394
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:39,829
I'll be waiting for you
at the new Tohyama Clinic.

395
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:47,837
Oh, you scared me.

396
00:25:50,131 --> 00:25:51,383
What's wrong?

397
00:25:52,342 --> 00:25:54,344
Me and my mom, we don't look alike, do we?

398
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,179
Oh. Well…

399
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:58,598
I mean, uh, we look alike, right?

400
00:25:58,682 --> 00:26:00,517
I know it's because Mom had work done.

401
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,935
Huh?

402
00:26:12,445 --> 00:26:14,739
I'M SORRY, ARATA

403
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:25,083
I LIED TO YOUR DAD,
YOUR GRANDMOTHER, AND YOU.

404
00:26:29,379 --> 00:26:33,758
ODAJIMA CONSTRUCTION COMPANY

405
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:36,177
We're all set here. Hey, stay back.

406
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:37,220
Mom?

407
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:40,265
- Hey, Mom! Mom!
- Arata! No.

408
00:26:40,348 --> 00:26:42,726
- Mom! Mom! Bring her back!
- Don't look!

409
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:43,893
- Stay here.
- Mom!

410
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:46,187
Mom! No!

411
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,522
Mom, wait!

412
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:54,529
I HOPE YOU WILL BE
A FINE HEIR TO THE ODAJIMA FAMILY.

413
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:57,449
SAYURI TOHYAMA

414
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:06,458
<i>So, he didn't give you a straight answer.</i>

415
00:27:06,541 --> 00:27:08,460
Is he your dad or not?

416
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:11,087
Mm, maybe, maybe not.

417
00:27:11,171 --> 00:27:12,505
Well, which is it?

418
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:13,965
Flip a coin!

419
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,344
You're messing with me…

420
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:21,681
Like, don't you need to know for sure,
one way or the other?

421
00:27:21,765 --> 00:27:22,849
Yeah, that'd be nice.

422
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:26,811
But he didn't give me a straight answer,
did he? Whatever.

423
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,606
Maybe I should threaten him
with a knife, huh?

424
00:27:30,106 --> 00:27:30,940
Another bottle?

425
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:34,903
Listen, Fumi.

426
00:27:34,986 --> 00:27:37,280
Your brother wanted you to quit, right?

427
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:39,366
You can't go back to the way things were.

428
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:41,660
Ah! Excuse me! Another bottle?

429
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:42,994
Right away, ma'am.

430
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,038
I'm gonna go home.

431
00:27:45,538 --> 00:27:46,665
Why?

432
00:27:46,748 --> 00:27:48,667
Because I have better things to do

433
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:51,544
than sit across
from an irresponsible drunk.

434
00:27:51,628 --> 00:27:53,254
I'm a what?

435
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:55,548
Things are tough for me right now!

436
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:58,343
- I'm just trying to survive here!
- Okay, fine. But let me ask you this.

437
00:27:58,426 --> 00:28:01,846
If the chairman does turn out
to be your real dad,

438
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:03,807
what will you do?

439
00:28:03,890 --> 00:28:07,143
You gonna keep it a secret from Rin
while you're working with her?

440
00:28:08,561 --> 00:28:10,980
Because you could, but that's not right.

441
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:15,735
That's not what a decent person would do.
Let's go!

442
00:29:31,227 --> 00:29:32,937
<i>You never valued me here.</i>

443
00:29:33,021 --> 00:29:35,315
I thought you'd make me
director of the Ginza clinic,

444
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,983
but you didn't want to promote me.

445
00:29:37,066 --> 00:29:40,153
<i>You just wanted to use me</i>
<i>to draw in female clients.</i>

446
00:29:41,863 --> 00:29:43,782
<i>Who's truly devious, then?</i>

447
00:29:44,365 --> 00:29:45,950
Don't pretend otherwise, Rin.

448
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:54,292
Why not give up the Tohyama name?

449
00:29:58,254 --> 00:30:00,924
- What are you talking about?
- Mm.

450
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:03,510
It could be a fresh start.

451
00:30:04,594 --> 00:30:07,514
What if you created a new name?
One that suited you better.

452
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:09,307
You could be free of him.

453
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:14,687
This public battle hurts you both,
and it doesn't do the clinic any good.

454
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:18,483
Tohyama is his mother's maiden name,
isn't it?

455
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:20,944
I doubt it means that much to you.

456
00:30:23,029 --> 00:30:24,531
And I doubt he'll give it up.

457
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:34,415
Tohyama's my name, and I'll keep it.

458
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:48,763
Here's the thing.

459
00:30:50,723 --> 00:30:52,809
My whole life I've wondered if I…

460
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:56,855
was truly worthy.

461
00:31:00,608 --> 00:31:02,819
I may not be his actual daughter,

462
00:31:03,319 --> 00:31:05,822
but they called me
the next Hand of God anyway.

463
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:10,076
I thought it was my destiny.

464
00:31:13,913 --> 00:31:16,082
I've been fighting to be accepted.

465
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:19,419
To be worthy of the title.

466
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:23,590
If I run away now…

467
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:29,345
I'm afraid I won't be me anymore.

468
00:31:29,429 --> 00:31:32,098
You know that's not true.
You've done great things.

469
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:33,766
- You're gonna keep doing them!
- It's okay.

470
00:31:35,101 --> 00:31:36,394
I've got Dr. Numata.

471
00:31:39,147 --> 00:31:40,815
And that means I can't lose.

472
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:51,159
Here you are.
Your patient list for the day.

473
00:31:51,242 --> 00:31:52,452
Whoa, that's a lot.

474
00:31:52,535 --> 00:31:54,370
It is, but you know about Dr. Rui?

475
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:58,082
Yeah, I get it.

476
00:31:58,166 --> 00:32:01,044
Oh, there was a request
that came in from a patient

477
00:32:01,127 --> 00:32:02,837
specifically for you, Doctor.

478
00:32:03,463 --> 00:32:04,422
For me?

479
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:09,928
It's been a while.

480
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:15,391
I have to say I was surprised.

481
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:18,353
About Dr. Rin's press conference.

482
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:23,232
Yeah, me too.
I was pretty surprised myself, honestly.

483
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,077
Do you remember what you said last time?

484
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:37,080
That I should go back to my original face.

485
00:32:37,163 --> 00:32:38,081
Yes.

486
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:40,041
That's what you told me to do.

487
00:32:41,584 --> 00:32:43,503
I still think about it sometimes.

488
00:32:46,130 --> 00:32:47,465
It was disrespectful.

489
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:50,051
I said some things I'm not proud of.
I'm sorry.

490
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:52,971
- But you've been successful regardless.
- I thank you for that.

491
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:03,773
How can I help you today, miss?

492
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:08,987
An endoscopic lift. I'd like to have one.

493
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,114
- You heard about that?
- I did.

494
00:33:11,739 --> 00:33:13,074
Dr. Rin sent me a text.

495
00:33:13,741 --> 00:33:15,284
You need a test subject.

496
00:33:16,202 --> 00:33:17,870
She had great things to say about you.

497
00:33:18,538 --> 00:33:22,333
Apparently, at the university hospital,
you were an endoscopic specialist.

498
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:24,419
That's a bit of an exaggeration.

499
00:33:24,502 --> 00:33:25,670
Maybe so.

500
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:29,549
Dr. Rin's never tried to sell me
on any treatments before.

501
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:31,843
So I knew.

502
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:34,387
I knew I had to make an appointment.

503
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:37,515
Yeah.

504
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:56,034
Hey.

505
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:58,202
I thought you quit.

506
00:34:00,246 --> 00:34:02,248
- Yeah, I probably should stop.
- Hey.

507
00:34:02,331 --> 00:34:04,292
- Maybe today's the day.
- Hey, it's fine, it's fine.

508
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:07,628
You've already got the pack out.
What's one cigarette? Go on.

509
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:11,132
- I can have one.
- Mm. Go for it.

510
00:34:13,551 --> 00:34:14,844
Yeah.

511
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:18,014
So you finally made your way out.

512
00:34:18,097 --> 00:34:20,391
No longer on the dark side, are ya?

513
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:24,771
- What about you, Doctor? Huh?
- Not a chance in hell.

514
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:29,817
You know, it's funny.

515
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:32,487
Dr. Rui actually made me an offer.

516
00:34:32,570 --> 00:34:34,572
"You wanna blow this popsicle stand?"

517
00:34:35,698 --> 00:34:37,533
- You serious? What will you do?
- Uh-huh.

518
00:34:37,617 --> 00:34:39,160
Too much trouble to quit now.

519
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:44,707
But then Dr. Rin got wind of it.

520
00:34:44,791 --> 00:34:49,045
I told her the whole thing,
and she offered me a raise.

521
00:34:50,671 --> 00:34:52,215
Nice. Nice.

522
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:54,342
Thank you.

523
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:56,969
And you,

524
00:34:57,970 --> 00:35:00,473
you're just as stuck here as I am now.

525
00:35:01,724 --> 00:35:02,558
Why's that?

526
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:04,519
Yeah. Endoscope's a big deal.

527
00:35:04,602 --> 00:35:08,314
They invested millions in it,
and now that pressure's on you.

528
00:35:11,150 --> 00:35:12,610
I'd hate that kinda thing.

529
00:35:12,693 --> 00:35:14,987
I don't have time for it.

530
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:16,614
Three kids, plus my wife.

531
00:35:17,990 --> 00:35:21,160
- You finding it kinda hot?
- Huh? Not at all.

532
00:35:22,703 --> 00:35:24,622
'Cause I am feeling thirsty.

533
00:35:24,705 --> 00:35:25,706
What?

534
00:35:26,874 --> 00:35:28,501
You inviting me out for a drink?

535
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:32,630
SNACK BAR ITTENBARI

536
00:35:32,713 --> 00:35:34,632
BACK IN BUSINESS
WE LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING YOU

537
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:41,097
- Yoko!
- Yoko, yeah!

538
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:46,519
<i>Don't it make me cry</i>

539
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:50,398
- Ooh!
- That's amazing!

540
00:35:51,732 --> 00:35:53,442
Hey. Hey! What's going on?

541
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:56,195
- Water, please.
- What?

542
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:58,197
- I said water now.
- Yeah, sure.

543
00:35:59,115 --> 00:36:00,032
Hey, what's wrong?

544
00:36:00,116 --> 00:36:01,701
Takeru here, or what?

545
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:03,953
Is Takeru here?

546
00:36:04,453 --> 00:36:06,789
Uh, he's, um…

547
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:09,250
- Upstairs?
- Probably, yeah.

548
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:10,793
Takeru.

549
00:36:11,752 --> 00:36:12,628
Takeru!

550
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,801
Hey! Takeru! You in there?

551
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:22,180
I gotta talk to you.

552
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:25,933
Takeru! We gotta talk! Open the door!

553
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:28,519
Hey, hey, no! Stop being so loud!

554
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:30,605
- Bastard.
- You're drunk.

555
00:36:31,105 --> 00:36:32,648
You wanted to talk!

556
00:36:32,732 --> 00:36:34,817
- Just leave him alone.
- Hey, open up! Come on, hey!

557
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:36,986
Fumi, you're so drunk!

558
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:39,822
Huh? Who cares about that?

559
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:42,283
We have to talk. Now.
So open the door! Come on!

560
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:43,784
Maybe come back tomorrow.

561
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:45,870
Get off. Nobody asked you, Macky!

562
00:36:45,953 --> 00:36:48,331
- That's enough.
- You're not part of this family.

563
00:36:48,414 --> 00:36:49,707
So shut the hell up!

564
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:52,752
What did you expect would happen?
You've been ignoring him.

565
00:36:54,795 --> 00:36:58,299
Nobody asked you. Now get the hell out.
You can't keep staying here!

566
00:36:58,382 --> 00:36:59,300
Stop, please. Stop.

567
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:00,676
That what you want? I'll leave.

568
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,470
- Get the hell out!
- But you're being awful.

569
00:37:02,553 --> 00:37:04,347
You're banging on his door, piss-drunk.

570
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:06,515
You're an asshole! You are!
You're being a shithead!

571
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:08,059
I don't need this from a freeloader!

572
00:37:08,142 --> 00:37:10,353
That's enough, you two!

573
00:37:10,853 --> 00:37:12,647
Back off and calm down!

574
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:18,152
Fumi, I get that you're going through
a lot right now,

575
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:21,280
but you're not the only one
who's grieving your mother's death.

576
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:26,452
I know I'm not your father,
and maybe it's not my place to say this,

577
00:37:27,036 --> 00:37:28,412
but you're out of control.

578
00:37:30,623 --> 00:37:34,377
Always coming home drunk,
lashing out at everyone.

579
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:36,629
Mommy was the same when things got bad.

580
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:41,634
I think it's time for you to leave, Fumi.

581
00:37:47,598 --> 00:37:48,557
Fine.

582
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:51,143
I'll be going, then.

583
00:37:55,398 --> 00:37:58,818
- <i>We have just received word…</i>
- Rin, come watch this.

584
00:37:58,901 --> 00:38:01,112
- He won.
<i>- …Ohkura has been projected to win.</i>

585
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:04,490
<i>What a comeback for Ohkura,</i>
<i>who many believed was at a disadvantage</i>

586
00:38:04,573 --> 00:38:08,244
<i>after spending much of</i>
<i>the election campaign in a hospital bed.</i>

587
00:38:08,327 --> 00:38:11,539
<i>A triumphant recovery</i>
<i>in more ways than one.</i>

588
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,208
- Let's have a toast.
- Yeah.

589
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:15,376
Be right back.

590
00:38:15,459 --> 00:38:18,629
<i>Your opponent</i>
<i>has raised concerns about your stamina.</i>

591
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:21,882
<i>I think my illness provided me</i>
<i>with a unique perspective</i>

592
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:24,010
<i>that will be useful in serving you all.</i>

593
00:38:24,093 --> 00:38:26,679
Besides, my doctors have given me
a clean bill of health.

594
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:28,180
It almost feels as though

595
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:32,184
the rest and recovery
have made me ten years younger.

596
00:38:33,769 --> 00:38:37,356
<i>It's my goal to make Tokyo</i>
<i>a world-class beauty hub,</i>

597
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:40,860
<i>and I believe</i>
<i>the public shares my enthusiasm.</i>

598
00:38:42,028 --> 00:38:45,698
<i>I want a future where people come</i>
<i>from all over the world to Tokyo</i>

599
00:38:45,781 --> 00:38:47,616
<i>in search of youth and beauty</i>

600
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:49,910
<i>because we're the best there is.</i>

601
00:38:56,208 --> 00:38:59,086
So, the accountant handed me this today.

602
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:01,964
It's a donation request from an orphanage.

603
00:39:04,467 --> 00:39:07,636
KOMADORI SEIAI INFANT HOME

604
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:11,599
- Is that from the orphanage?
- Yeah.

605
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:13,768
Guess it's that time of year again, huh?

606
00:39:14,477 --> 00:39:15,436
- It is.
- Hmm.

607
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:17,480
<i>You've been making donations every year?</i>

608
00:39:17,563 --> 00:39:19,899
This is the first I'm hearing about it.

609
00:39:19,982 --> 00:39:21,108
Hmm.

610
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:24,987
They were good to me a long time ago.

611
00:39:25,738 --> 00:39:26,989
I don't know.

612
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,617
Maybe it's been long enough.

613
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:31,160
Are you sure?

614
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:33,412
I mean, it is a wonderful cause.

615
00:39:34,121 --> 00:39:37,291
Well, it's been a long time.

616
00:39:37,375 --> 00:39:38,626
Over 30 years, in fact.

617
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:41,796
Whatever you want. I'll let them know.

618
00:39:43,297 --> 00:39:44,965
DONATION APPLICATION FORM

619
00:39:47,843 --> 00:39:50,971
DONATION AMOUNT: ¥1,000,000

620
00:39:52,431 --> 00:39:53,808
- Hey.
- Hmm?

621
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:57,103
- It's time for the toast.
- Sorry, you're right.

622
00:39:57,603 --> 00:39:58,604
Here.

623
00:40:00,147 --> 00:40:02,900
- So, here's to you.
- Thank you.

624
00:40:06,737 --> 00:40:08,906
LETTERS FROM FORMER RESIDENTS

625
00:40:08,989 --> 00:40:10,116
KOMADORI SEIAI INFANT HOME

626
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:13,119
- She's beautiful.
- She really is.

627
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:16,080
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

628
00:40:16,914 --> 00:40:17,998
<i>She's a miracle.</i>

629
00:40:18,791 --> 00:40:21,544
The Tohyama name is hers now.

630
00:40:44,692 --> 00:40:47,027
<i>I guess that means</i>
<i>you're going to get busy again?</i>

631
00:40:48,904 --> 00:40:50,656
I am.

632
00:40:50,739 --> 00:40:52,032
I've got some charcuterie.

633
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,742
- Oh, thank you.
- You want some?

634
00:40:54,952 --> 00:40:57,163
If you don't mind waiting,
the doctor should be here soon.

635
00:40:57,246 --> 00:40:58,247
Sure.

636
00:40:58,330 --> 00:40:59,206
Hi.

637
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:00,833
- Good morning.
- Morning.

638
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:03,836
Will you tell us
where you'd like the machine installed?

639
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:06,380
Mm…

640
00:41:06,464 --> 00:41:10,342
It's your baby, after all.
You're going to do great things with it.

641
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:15,264
You okay?

642
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:18,142
Are you getting enough sleep?

643
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:21,270
Yeah. Anyway, over there.

644
00:41:21,353 --> 00:41:22,563
Sure thing.

645
00:41:22,646 --> 00:41:24,148
Uh, right up against the wall.

646
00:42:12,905 --> 00:42:15,866
- Sorry about that.
- Are you sure you're not too tired?

647
00:42:16,367 --> 00:42:17,451
I told you I'm fine.

648
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:19,912
Hang on. I'll handle this one.

649
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:22,248
- Huh?
- You can assist me this time.

650
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:24,333
Why? I'm fine.

651
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:25,668
You're not fine.

652
00:42:25,751 --> 00:42:28,003
I could smell the alcohol
on you this morning.

653
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:30,589
You need to take better care of yourself.

654
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:15,092
I, um… I'm sorry.

655
00:43:15,175 --> 00:43:17,052
Don't worry. It's over now.

656
00:43:17,803 --> 00:43:20,055
I just need you
to be at the post-op review.

657
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:24,143
Director.

658
00:43:28,731 --> 00:43:30,024
Uh…

659
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:33,652
- What is it?
- Nothing.

660
00:43:35,404 --> 00:43:36,280
Nothing.

661
00:43:38,407 --> 00:43:39,575
I'm really sorry.

662
00:43:57,301 --> 00:44:00,471
<i>Now, your recovery time begins.</i>
<i>Two weeks in your chrysalis.</i>

663
00:44:01,388 --> 00:44:03,140
It's very important to rest.

664
00:44:03,641 --> 00:44:06,560
See, a butterfly needs recovery time
in its chrysalis

665
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:09,271
before it can transform
into something new.

666
00:44:17,237 --> 00:44:18,197
Takeru.

667
00:44:20,074 --> 00:44:23,994
<i>It's completely normal to experience</i>
<i>growing pains during this period.</i>

668
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:27,081
<i>Change can be scary.</i>

669
00:44:27,164 --> 00:44:31,210
<i>But just imagine how wonderful it will be</i>
<i>to spread your beautiful new wings</i>

670
00:44:31,293 --> 00:44:33,545
<i>and fly towards the future you dream of.</i>

671
00:44:34,588 --> 00:44:36,882
We'll get through the tough part together.

672
00:44:36,965 --> 00:44:38,592
<i>We'll get you to the other side.</i>

673
00:44:39,593 --> 00:44:41,345
The new you is almost here.

674
00:44:42,846 --> 00:44:46,684
In your case, Ms. Shimizu,
the swelling should be significantly…

675
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:49,478
- Doctor, there's a call from home for you.
- What?

676
00:44:49,561 --> 00:44:51,355
The results will be worth it.

677
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:53,482
The previous procedure
is taking longer than expected.

678
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:56,193
We're very sorry.
We're expecting an update for you soon.

679
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:57,778
If you would wait here.

680
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:04,201
- Takeru, you need to hold still!
- Calm down!

681
00:45:04,284 --> 00:45:05,828
- Let go!
- It's dangerous!

682
00:45:05,911 --> 00:45:07,913
- I don't want your help!
- Don't move. Let me look!

683
00:45:07,996 --> 00:45:09,873
- Calm down.
- Stay still!

684
00:45:10,374 --> 00:45:12,543
I can't work if you fight me!

685
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:15,254
Damn it!
Why would you do this to yourself?

686
00:45:15,337 --> 00:45:16,880
Like you'd even understand!

687
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:17,798
What?

688
00:45:17,881 --> 00:45:20,300
Mom got plastic surgery, didn't she?

689
00:45:20,384 --> 00:45:22,136
I just wanna look like her!

690
00:45:25,305 --> 00:45:27,683
Come on, let me go.

691
00:45:31,228 --> 00:45:32,604
Thanks, both of you.

692
00:45:33,355 --> 00:45:35,482
- It's okay. I've got it.
- Okay.

693
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:48,036
Takeru.

694
00:46:00,132 --> 00:46:01,550
I'm so sorry.

695
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,807
You're right, I didn't understand.

696
00:46:13,145 --> 00:46:14,980
I was scared and lost.

697
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:17,983
I didn't know how to cope.

698
00:46:20,319 --> 00:46:22,154
So I just avoided facing it at all.

699
00:46:25,324 --> 00:46:26,950
I'm sorry, Takeru.

700
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:30,829
I'm sorry.

701
00:46:36,710 --> 00:46:38,545
I'll never let you down again, okay?

702
00:46:42,049 --> 00:46:43,926
I'm gonna tell you everything.

703
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:48,931
Would you please let me treat you?

704
00:46:49,765 --> 00:46:50,682
Please?

705
00:46:54,686 --> 00:46:55,896
What do you say?

706
00:47:12,079 --> 00:47:13,247
Um…

707
00:47:15,249 --> 00:47:17,125
Do you really want this surgery?

708
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:23,841
You tried to tell me before.

709
00:47:28,428 --> 00:47:30,138
But I didn't listen, and I should have.

710
00:47:36,770 --> 00:47:37,729
Look.

711
00:47:39,147 --> 00:47:42,985
If this is something you really want,
then I'll do it for you.

712
00:47:49,783 --> 00:47:51,076
It's your decision.

713
00:47:52,828 --> 00:47:53,829
I want…

714
00:47:58,166 --> 00:47:59,835
I want to change.

715
00:48:02,462 --> 00:48:05,090
I wanna do it. I want to be someone new.

716
00:48:08,093 --> 00:48:10,596
Even with plastic surgery,
you're still Takeru.

717
00:48:10,679 --> 00:48:11,847
I know.

718
00:48:13,515 --> 00:48:15,309
But I still wanna change.

719
00:48:22,482 --> 00:48:23,400
Okay.

720
00:48:26,320 --> 00:48:27,946
Leave it to me. I've got you.

721
00:48:30,908 --> 00:48:32,242
It hurts, huh?

722
00:48:35,245 --> 00:48:37,706
Do you mind
if I perform the procedure by myself?

723
00:48:39,207 --> 00:48:40,292
It's fine.

724
00:48:44,254 --> 00:48:45,839
Okay, let's get started.

725
00:48:56,767 --> 00:48:58,727
Yeah, this part stings.

726
00:49:02,022 --> 00:49:03,565
- Hang in there.
- Mm-hmm.

727
00:49:03,649 --> 00:49:05,651
Hang in there. I've got you.

728
00:49:05,734 --> 00:49:08,028
I know it's uncomfortable.

729
00:49:08,612 --> 00:49:10,238
We're gonna get through this.

730
00:49:18,121 --> 00:49:20,749
Okay, this is gonna sting a little.

731
00:49:23,085 --> 00:49:23,961
There.

732
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:26,964
You won't feel the next one.

733
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:31,093
- No pain, right?
- Mm.

734
00:49:36,139 --> 00:49:38,183
And now? Feeling any pressure?

735
00:49:38,684 --> 00:49:40,227
- I'm okay.
- Yeah? You sure?

736
00:50:21,309 --> 00:50:23,562
DEAR DR. RIN TOHYAMA

737
00:50:33,405 --> 00:50:36,033
- Director.
- Ah, good morning. Is something wrong?

738
00:50:36,116 --> 00:50:38,452
It's the endoscopic surgeries.

739
00:50:39,453 --> 00:50:41,079
The bookings are really taking off.

740
00:50:58,013 --> 00:50:59,848
FROM: FUMI NUMATA
SEND

741
00:51:17,199 --> 00:51:18,075
Hey.

742
00:51:20,619 --> 00:51:22,204
What? Are you still mad at me?

743
00:51:23,205 --> 00:51:25,957
No. Of course not. I'm not mad at you.

744
00:51:26,500 --> 00:51:29,669
- You're obviously mad.
- I'm not mad. I've never been mad.

745
00:51:29,753 --> 00:51:30,921
You know what?

746
00:51:31,421 --> 00:51:34,674
You used to threaten my whole family.
What I did was nothing.

747
00:51:36,426 --> 00:51:37,469
Right?

748
00:51:43,558 --> 00:51:44,851
Did you two talk?

749
00:51:45,352 --> 00:51:46,561
You and Takeru?

750
00:51:53,777 --> 00:51:54,611
Look.

751
00:51:57,531 --> 00:51:59,282
Can't you tell what happened from my face?

752
00:52:05,372 --> 00:52:07,457
Your face looks the same
as it always does.

753
00:52:09,251 --> 00:52:10,752
Hey, can I get on this thing?

754
00:52:11,920 --> 00:52:13,213
Sure, go ahead.

755
00:52:14,256 --> 00:52:15,715
Okay.

756
00:52:16,258 --> 00:52:17,467
It's nice.

757
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:20,303
I wanna drive to the sea.

758
00:52:21,263 --> 00:52:23,056
- You mean today?
- Mm.

759
00:52:23,682 --> 00:52:25,767
- I just want to.
- Huh? Why the sea though?

760
00:52:27,185 --> 00:52:28,311
Can you take me there?

761
00:52:33,692 --> 00:52:36,611
- Doesn't this thing go any faster?
- Yeah, it goes faster.

762
00:52:36,695 --> 00:52:39,239
- You want faster? Hold on.
- Okay, I take it back. Wait!

763
00:52:43,243 --> 00:52:47,205
Oh, Director. Governor Ohkura
contacted us earlier today.

764
00:52:47,289 --> 00:52:50,167
He was hoping to come by for maintenance
and join you for dinner.

765
00:52:50,250 --> 00:52:51,751
Ah, wonderful.

766
00:52:52,252 --> 00:52:54,421
It's about time
the governor met Dr. Numata.

767
00:52:54,504 --> 00:52:56,381
Would you let him know
I'll be bringing a guest?

768
00:52:56,464 --> 00:52:57,966
Certainly, Director.

769
00:53:11,479 --> 00:53:13,773
FUMI NUMATA
(NO SUBJECT)

770
00:53:20,197 --> 00:53:21,823
<i>To Ms. Rin Tohyama.</i>

771
00:53:22,574 --> 00:53:25,160
<i>This may seem out of the blue,</i>
<i>and I apologize.</i>

772
00:53:27,078 --> 00:53:30,290
<i>But there's something I have to tell you,</i>

773
00:53:30,373 --> 00:53:31,458
<i>and it can't wait.</i>

774
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:39,090
There it is! The sea! Check it out.
Fumi! Look, look, look, look, over there!

775
00:53:39,174 --> 00:53:40,091
There it is!

776
00:53:40,175 --> 00:53:43,929
<i>I'm afraid I won't have the courage</i>
<i>to tell you in person.</i>

777
00:53:44,888 --> 00:53:46,848
<i>So I'm writing to you instead.</i>

778
00:53:50,018 --> 00:53:51,353
The sea!

779
00:53:51,436 --> 00:53:53,480
The sea!

780
00:53:54,481 --> 00:53:56,900
- Here we are!
- Here we are!

781
00:53:56,983 --> 00:53:58,568
- Hey, check out that bird!
- Where?

782
00:53:58,652 --> 00:54:01,029
- Look, it's massive!
- What the heck is that? It's huge!

783
00:54:01,112 --> 00:54:03,573
- I wouldn't get too close.
- Gosh! We're really here!

784
00:54:03,657 --> 00:54:04,991
<i>He hasn't admitted it yet,</i>

785
00:54:06,868 --> 00:54:08,620
<i>but I know what I know.</i>

786
00:54:10,997 --> 00:54:12,916
<i>Chairman Arata Tohyama…</i>

787
00:54:16,628 --> 00:54:18,296
<i>…is my biological father.</i>

788
00:54:21,549 --> 00:54:25,971
<i>I think it's time that I step away</i>
<i>from the world of cosmetic surgery.</i>

789
00:54:31,893 --> 00:54:33,478
MY LONG-LOST FATHER

790
00:54:43,613 --> 00:54:45,740
No. No, no.

791
00:54:45,824 --> 00:54:48,243
No! No! No, no! No!

792
00:54:48,326 --> 00:54:50,578
No, no! No! No!

793
00:54:50,662 --> 00:54:52,998
No!
